{"path":"experimental/optional/swap","title":"std::experimental::optional<T>::swap","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::optional&lt;T&gt;::</span>swap","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/optional/swap","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Swaps the contents with those of other.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> swap<span class=\"br0\">(</span> optional<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> other <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/* see below */</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Swaps the contents with those of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>.\n</p>\n<ul><li> If neither <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> nor <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> contain a value, the function has no effect.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li> If only one of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> contains a value (let's call this object <code>in</code> and the other <code>un</code>), the contained value of <code>un</code> is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/direct_initialization\">direct-initialized</a> from <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">move</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>in<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, followed by destruction of the contained value of <code>in</code> as if by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">in.<span class=\"me1\">val</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>T<span class=\"sy4\">::</span>~T<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. After this call, <code>in</code> does not contain a value <code>un</code> contains a value.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li> If both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> contain values, the contained values are exchanged by calling <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/swap\"><span class=\"kw1611\">std::<span class=\"me2\">swap</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> swap<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">**</span>this, <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>other<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>. <code>T</code> lvalues must satisfy <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Swappable\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Swappable</em></a>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> other\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the <code>optional</code> object to exchange the contents with\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-noexcept-full\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;\n<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_move_constructible\"><span class=\"kw549\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_nothrow_move_constructible</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>swap<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/declval\"><span class=\"kw1128\">std::<span class=\"me2\">declval</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/declval\"><span class=\"kw1128\">std::<span class=\"me2\">declval</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></span></div></div>\n<p>In the case of thrown exception, the states of the contained values of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code> are determined by the exception safety guarantees of <code>swap</code> of type <code>T</code> or <code>T</code>'s move constructor, whichever is called. For both <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">other</span></code>, if the object contained a value, it is left containing a value, and the other way round.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/optional/swap2\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>std::swap<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::experimental::optional)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  specializes the <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/swap\">std::swap</a></span> algorithm <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/optional","title":"std::experimental::optional"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::optional<T>::swap","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Swaps the contents with those of other."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"other"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"In the case of thrown exception, the states of the contained values of *this and other are determined by the exception safety guarantees of swap of type T or…"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"std::swap(std::experimental::optional)","note":"specializes the std::swap algorithm"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":195,"codeBlockCount":0}
